{"t": 1794105763.3729088, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "*PaymentGatewayErrors checkout (AG-7731)* \u2014 root cause identified, fix ready.\n\nWhat broke: at 07:41 UTC the payment gateway switched to API 2026-11 (strict amounts). Checkout was sending `amount` as a decimal EUR value (`12.34`), which the gateway now rejects with `400 invalid_amount` (\"amount must be an integer in minor units (cents)\"). That drove the gateway 4xx rate to 38%.\n\nFix: `checkout/gateway.py::charge_payload` now converts EUR to integer cents (Decimal, half-up) and sends `{\"amount\": 1234, \"currency\": \"EUR\"}`. Verified locally for 12.34 -> 1234, 19.99 -> 1999, 1234.56 -> 123456. No test suite in the repo (`pytest` collects nothing), so verification was a direct call of the function.\n\nNext: deploy checkout with the patch and watch gateway 4xx rate drop below threshold; then resolve AG-7731."}, "ok": true}
